{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-09-24T17:12:44.146Z","data":{"text":"Task complete.\n\n**What I did:**\n\n1. **Tests first** — created `tests/status-drift-cli.test.ts` (new file, allowed) with one `FakeRuntime`, `FakeClock`, and `FakeCaddyAdmin`, covering each acceptance line:\n   - healthy container → empty stderr\n   - disappeared container → exact 1-item warning, stdout table unchanged, state stays `running`\n   - `status --json` / `status web --json` → byte-identical stdout + warning\n   - orphan + disappeared container → 2-item warning\n   - `runtime.unavailable` → table, empty stderr, exit 0; `status nope` still fails with the unknown-app error\n\n2. **Modified `tests/status-logs-cli.test.ts`** — only the one assertion named in the task Context, in \"status prints the aligned overview with uptime and dashes\".\n\n3. **Implemented `src/commands/status.ts`** — added a best-effort `warnDrift` called after normal output for both `paas status` and `paas status <app>`, inside the same `withStore`. It pings the runtime, runs `runReconcile` in dry-run mode, and writes the warning to `io.err` when items exist. All errors (including the synchronous `getRuntime` socket failure) are swallowed. Unknown apps still fail before any check.\n\n**Verification:**\n- Task verify `node --import tsx --test tests/status-drift-cli.test.ts`: 5/5 pass\n- Proposal verify `pnpm verify`: 373/373 pass (typecheck + full suite), including `status-logs-cli.test.ts` and `deploy-cli.test.ts` unchanged in behavior\n\nResult written to `openspec/changes/011-reconcile/.run/results/3.md`."}}
